  "place": "Berkeley, United States",
  "nameOrigin": "After Berkeley, California, where it was made, in the way terbium was named after Ytterby.",
  "source": "pubchem",
  "note": "Made in December 1949 by alpha bombardment of americium-241 and published in 1950 (Phys. Rev. 77, 838). Jefferson Lab also lists Kenneth Street Jr., who is not an author of the discovery paper.",
